  "sentences": [
    {
      "id": 1,
      "text": "Nature is amazing!",
      "file": "assets/audio/sentences/sentence-01.mp3",
      "exists": true
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Take a close look at the world of insects, and you'll discover many unbelievable things.",
      "file": "assets/audio/sentences/sentence-02.mp3",
      "exists": true
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Consider butterflies.",
      "file": "assets/audio/sentences/sentence-03.mp3",
      "exists": true
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "They have beautiful, colourful wings, and strong, fantastic flying skills.",
      "file": "assets/audio/sentences/sentence-04.mp3",
      "exists": true
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "On summer days, you always see them flying freely over gardens and wild fields.",
      "file": "assets/audio/sentences/sentence-05.mp3",
      "exists": true
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "How a butterfly appears is one of the amazing wonders of nature.",
      "file": "assets/audio/sentences/sentence-06.mp3",
      "exists": true
    },
    {
      "id": 7,
      "text": "In the beginning, female butterflies lay a small egg on a leaf or stem of a plant.",
      "file": "assets/audio/sentences/sentence-07.mp3",
      "exists": true
    },
    {
      "id": 8,
      "text": "The egg will become something completely different in a few days.",
      "file": "assets/audio/sentences/sentence-08.mp3",
      "exists": true
    },
    {
      "id": 9,
      "text": "It first becomes a walking insect called caterpillar.",
      "file": "assets/audio/sentences/sentence-09.mp3",
      "exists": true
    },
    {
      "id": 10,
      "text": "It then has legs, eyes and a body that looks fat.",
      "file": "assets/audio/sentences/sentence-10.mp3",
      "exists": true
    },
    {
      "id": 11,
      "text": "But it is still not a butterfly.",
      "file": "assets/audio/sentences/sentence-11.mp3",
      "exists": true
    },
    {
      "id": 12,
      "text": "Soon, after growing big, the caterpillar produces silk threads to make a cover for itself.",
      "file": "assets/audio/sentences/sentence-12.mp3",
      "exists": true
    },
    {
      "id": 13,
      "text": "It covers itself in a nice protective blanket to go to sleep.",
      "file": "assets/audio/sentences/sentence-13.mp3",
      "exists": true
    },
    {
      "id": 14,
      "text": "It ties itself to a leaf or a branch, where it is not easy for birds to find.",
      "file": "assets/audio/sentences/sentence-14.mp3",
      "exists": true
    },
    {
      "id": 15,
      "text": "This stage is known as the pupa stage.",
      "file": "assets/audio/sentences/sentence-15.mp3",
      "exists": true
    },
    {
      "id": 16,
      "text": "The pupa stays shut until it finishes the transformation.",
      "file": "assets/audio/sentences/sentence-16.mp3",
      "exists": true
    },
    {
      "id": 17,
      "text": "After a period of time, the blanket breaks and a wet, weak butterfly appears.",
      "file": "assets/audio/sentences/sentence-17.mp3",
      "exists": true
    },
    {
      "id": 18,
      "text": "It may look ugly at first, but shortly, the wings fill with blood, and the beautiful, colourful butterfly spreads its wings.",
      "file": "assets/audio/sentences/sentence-18.mp3",
      "exists": true
    },
    {
      "id": 19,
      "text": "Now this insect can fly to the left and to the right to look for food and a partner.",
      "file": "assets/audio/sentences/sentence-19.mp3",
      "exists": true
    },
    {
      "id": 20,
      "text": "After a few weeks, this adult butterfly lays her eggs, and the cycle begins all over again.",
      "file": "assets/audio/sentences/sentence-20.mp3",
      "exists": true
    }
  ],
